<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dilip Singh Judeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/2013">2013</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dilip Singh Judeo was an Indian politician from the former royal family of Jashpur in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>. A leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bharatiya-janata-party">Bharatiya Janata Party</a>, he served in both houses of Parliament and as a minister of state in the national government in 2003. He was known for his campaigns to reconvert Christian Adivasis to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a>.</p></div>
